In article <2759@pur-phy> sho@maxwell.physics.purdue.edu.UUCP (Sho Kuwamoto) writes:
>3) Someone else said something about water.  I hope the intention was
>not to have drinking water be as essential as eating food....

I think that was me.  I was just pointing out that in a real survival
situation, water is much more important than food.  And since the
adventurer doesn't ever sleep in Hack, it seems odd that he needs to
be eating all the time.  A better game would have the adventurer
needing water instead of food.  I'm not suggesting this change for
Nethack, just commenting.

In another article, someone suggested "going down slowly" as the best
hint for doing well at Nethack.  That's certainly true, but the need
for food pressures the player into descending more quickly than he'd
like, especially for characters that start with little or no food.
That's going to become even worse if the % of time that a monster
leaves behind a corpse is reduced (as I surmise it was in PL 5?).  The
Nethack designers need to be careful with this type of change, because
it affects the game balance much more drastically than you might
expect.

